      "Empty web pages and browser-based technologies input is handled gracefully and returns an appropriate empty-state message or default output",
      "Mixed encoding input is normalized to UTF-8 before processing to prevent character corruption in multi-language environments",
      "Very large inputs exceeding 100 MB are processed in streaming chunks to avoid blocking the browser event loop",
      "Deeply nested web pages and browser-based technologies structures beyond 50 levels trigger a recursion-depth warning before processing begins",
      "Input containing special characters (emoji, diacritics, Unicode) is processed correctly per web standards",
      "Concurrent processing of multiple items in batch mode maintains correct ordering of outputs relative to inputs",
      "Trailing whitespace and empty lines in the input are stripped before processing to avoid silent mismatches",
      "Duplicate entries in lists or arrays are preserved unless an explicit deduplication feature is invoked",
      "Malformed BOM (Byte Order Mark) at the start of input is automatically detected and stripped",
      "Timezone information in timestamps is preserved and not silently converted to local time",
